1
00:00:00,751 --> 00:00:03,253
( all groaning )

2
00:00:05,464 --> 00:00:07,299
OH, MONICA,
THAT WAS THE BEST

3
00:00:07,299 --> 00:00:08,968
THANKSGIVING DINNER EVER.

4
00:00:08,968 --> 00:00:10,385
IT WAS SO GOOD.

5
00:00:10,385 --> 00:00:11,720
I THINK YOU KILLED US.

6
00:00:13,305 --> 00:00:15,766
I COULDN'T POSSIBLY
EAT ANOTHER BITE.

7
00:00:15,766 --> 00:00:19,436
I NEED SOMETHING SWEET.

8
00:00:19,436 --> 00:00:21,188
DOES ANYONE WANT TO WATCH TV?

9
00:00:21,188 --> 00:00:22,481
All:
YEAH.

10
00:00:24,441 --> 00:00:27,277
MONICA, YOUR REMOTE
DOESN'T WORK.

11
00:00:27,277 --> 00:00:30,614
PHOEBE, YOU HAVE
TO LIFT IT AND POINT.

12
00:00:30,614 --> 00:00:33,033
OH.

13
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:35,327
OH, FORGET IT.

14
00:00:35,327 --> 00:00:37,538
HEY, YOU KNOW WHAT
WE SHOULD ALL DO?

15
00:00:37,538 --> 00:00:39,414
WE SHOULD PLAY THAT GAME
WHERE EVERYONE SAYS

16
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:41,124
ONE THING THAT
THEY'RE THANKFUL FOR.

17
00:00:41,124 --> 00:00:43,168
OH, I... I AM THANKFUL

18
00:00:43,168 --> 00:00:46,087
FOR THIS BEAUTIFUL FALL
WE'VE BEEN HAVING.

19
00:00:46,087 --> 00:00:47,923
THAT'S SWEET, JOEY.
VERY NICE.

20
00:00:47,923 --> 00:00:50,175
YEAH, THE OTHER DAY
I WAS AT THE BUS STOP

21
00:00:50,175 --> 00:00:52,970
AND THIS LOVELY FALL BREEZE
CAME IN OUT OF NOWHERE

22
00:00:52,970 --> 00:00:54,972
AND BLEW THIS CHICK'S SKIRT
RIGHT UP.

23
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:57,933
OH, WHICH REMINDS ME

24
00:00:57,933 --> 00:01:00,728
I'M ALSO THANKFUL FOR THONGS.

25
00:01:07,693 --> 00:01:09,069
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU ♪

26
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:12,698
♪ LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

27
00:01:12,698 --> 00:01:15,075
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

28
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:17,995
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

29
00:01:17,995 --> 00:01:22,416
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

30
00:01:22,416 --> 00:01:24,501
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

31
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:27,421
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

32
00:01:27,421 --> 00:01:31,050
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

33
00:01:31,050 --> 00:01:33,176
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

34
00:01:33,176 --> 00:01:35,763
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

35
00:01:35,763 --> 00:01:38,015
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

36
00:01:38,015 --> 00:01:41,184
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

37
00:01:41,184 --> 00:01:44,730
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

38
00:01:51,070 --> 00:01:53,196
I MEAN, IT'S NOT 
SO MUCH AN UNDERPANT

39
00:01:53,196 --> 00:01:56,533
AS IT IS A FEAT OF ENGINEERING.

40
00:01:56,533 --> 00:01:58,702
IT'S AMAZING
HOW MUCH THEY CAN DO

41
00:01:58,702 --> 00:02:01,080
WITH SO LITTLE MATERIAL.

42
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:02,664
YOU KNOW, AND THE WAY
THEY PLAY WITH YOUR MIND.

43
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:04,625
I MEAN, IS IT THERE?
IS IT NOT THERE?

44
00:02:04,625 --> 00:02:06,125
( mumbling )

45
00:02:06,125 --> 00:02:09,922
ARE YOU AWARE THAT
YOU'RE STILL TALKING?

46
00:02:09,922 --> 00:02:11,673
IS ANYONE THANKFUL
FOR ANYTHING ELSE

47
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:13,884
BESIDES A THONG?

48
00:02:13,884 --> 00:02:15,135
HUH, I DON'T KNOW
WHAT TO PICK.

49
00:02:15,135 --> 00:02:16,929
AM I MORE THANKFUL
FOR MY DIVORCE

50
00:02:16,929 --> 00:02:18,346
OR MY EVICTION?

51
00:02:18,346 --> 00:02:19,765
WOW. SEE, AND I DIDN'T THINK

52
00:02:19,765 --> 00:02:21,725
YOU'D BE ABLE TO COME UP
WITH ANYTHING.

53
00:02:24,185 --> 00:02:27,272
I'M SORRY, IT'S JUST
THIS IS THE WORST
THANKSGIVING EVER.

54
00:02:27,272 --> 00:02:29,900
NO, NO, NO, NO. I AM THE KING
OF BAD THANKSGIVINGS.

55
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:31,819
YOU CAN'T JUST SWOOP IN HERE
WITH YOUR BAD MARRIAGE

56
00:02:31,819 --> 00:02:34,113
AND TAKE THAT AWAY FROM ME.

57
00:02:34,113 --> 00:02:35,823
NO, YOU'RE NOT GOING TO TELL
THE WHOLE STORY

58
00:02:35,823 --> 00:02:37,532
ABOUT HOW YOUR PARENTS
GOT DIVORCED AGAIN, ARE YOU?

59
00:02:37,532 --> 00:02:38,826
OH, GOD NO.

60
00:02:38,826 --> 00:02:41,954
NO, NO, COME ON,
I WANT TO HEAR IT.

61
00:02:43,956 --> 00:02:48,794
IT WOULDN'T BE THANKSGIVING
WITHOUT CHANDLER BUMMING US OUT.

62
00:02:48,794 --> 00:02:50,712
IT'S A TRADITION
LIKE THE PARADE...

63
00:02:50,712 --> 00:02:52,881
IF THE PARADE DECIDED
IT WAS GAY, MOVED OUT

64
00:02:52,881 --> 00:02:55,258
AND ABANDONED
ITS ENTIRE FAMILY.

65
00:02:57,970 --> 00:03:00,388
NOW, CHANDLER, DEAR,
JUST BECAUSE

66
00:03:00,388 --> 00:03:02,181
YOUR FATHER AND I
ARE GETTING A DIVORCE

67
00:03:02,181 --> 00:03:04,559
DOESN'T MEAN
WE DON'T LOVE YOU.

68
00:03:04,559 --> 00:03:06,895
IT JUST MEANS
HE WOULD RATHER SLEEP

69
00:03:06,895 --> 00:03:10,065
WITH THE HOUSEBOY
THAN WITH ME.

70
00:03:12,233 --> 00:03:14,653
MORE TURKEY,
MR. CHANDLER?

71
00:03:18,365 --> 00:03:20,199
YOU'RE RIGHT,
YOURS IS WORSE.

72
00:03:20,199 --> 00:03:22,744
YOU ARE THE KING OF
BAD THANKSGIVINGS.

73
00:03:22,744 --> 00:03:25,330
I DON'T KNOW ABOUT THAT.
I'VE GOT ONE THAT'S WORSE.

74
00:03:25,330 --> 00:03:28,667
REALLY? WORSE THAN
"MORE TURKEY, MR. CHANDLER?"

75
00:03:30,502 --> 00:03:32,046
OH, DID THE
LITTLE RICH BOY

76
00:03:32,046 --> 00:03:33,380
HAVE A PROBLEM
WITH THE BUTLER?

77
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:34,923
YES, MINE'S WORSE.

78
00:03:40,971 --> 00:03:44,516
MORE BANDAGES! MORE BANDAGES!

79
00:03:44,516 --> 00:03:47,853
PLEASE, CAN I GET
SOME MORE BANDAGES IN HERE?!

80
00:03:47,853 --> 00:03:49,604
THIS MAN IS DYING!

81
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:55,318
OH, NO.

82
00:03:58,655 --> 00:04:02,034
IN THIS LIFE, PHOEBE.

83
00:04:02,034 --> 00:04:03,660
OH, THIS LIFE.
OH, OKAY.

84
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:04,995
NO, CHANDLER'S IS WORSE.

85
00:04:06,621 --> 00:04:07,831
MAN, IT MUST
BE SO COOL,

86
00:04:07,831 --> 00:04:09,290
REMEMBERING STUFF
LIKE THAT.

87
00:04:09,290 --> 00:04:12,920
I DON'T HAVE ANY
PAST LIFE MEMORIES.

88
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:14,046
OF COURSE YOU
DON'T, SWEETIE.

89
00:04:14,046 --> 00:04:15,338
YOU'RE BRAND NEW.

90
00:04:17,549 --> 00:04:19,968
I KNOW MONICA'S
WORST THANKSGIVING.

91
00:04:19,968 --> 00:04:21,595
LET'S NOT TELL
THIS STORY.

92
00:04:21,595 --> 00:04:22,721
OH, COME ON.

93
00:04:22,721 --> 00:04:24,347
OH, NO. I KNOW,
I KNOW.

94
00:04:24,347 --> 00:04:25,807
IT'S THE ONE WHERE JOEY

95
00:04:25,807 --> 00:04:29,269
GOT MONICA'S TURKEY
STUCK ON HIS HEAD.

96
00:04:29,269 --> 00:04:30,604
WHAT?
WHAT?!

97
00:04:30,604 --> 00:04:33,481
JOEY GOT A TURKEY
STUCK ON HIS HEAD?

98
00:04:33,481 --> 00:04:35,067
HEY, IT'S NOT
LIKE IT SOUNDS.

99
00:04:35,067 --> 00:04:37,277
IT'S EXACTLY LIKE IT SOUNDS.

100
00:04:44,284 --> 00:04:45,284
( muffled ):
HELLO?

101
00:04:47,621 --> 00:04:51,917
HELLO?

102
00:04:51,917 --> 00:04:53,835
( muffled ):
PHOEBE?

103
00:04:53,835 --> 00:04:56,713
JOEY? WHAT'S GOING ON?

104
00:04:56,713 --> 00:04:59,424
( Phoebe gasps )

105
00:04:59,424 --> 00:05:00,926
OH, MY GOD!

106
00:05:00,926 --> 00:05:02,301
I KNOW.

107
00:05:02,301 --> 00:05:05,931
IT'S STUCK!

108
00:05:05,931 --> 00:05:08,600
STEP.
HOW DID IT GET ON?

109
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:11,645
I PUT IT ON
TO SCARE CHANDLER.

110
00:05:11,645 --> 00:05:13,063
OH, MY GOD!

111
00:05:13,063 --> 00:05:15,315
MONICA'S GOING TO
TOTALLY FREAK OUT.

112
00:05:15,315 --> 00:05:17,151
WELL, THEN HELP ME
GET IT OFF.

113
00:05:17,151 --> 00:05:19,945
PLUS, IT SMELLS
REALLY BAD IN HERE.

114
00:05:19,945 --> 00:05:22,030
OF COURSE IT
SMELLS REALLY BAD.

115
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:25,366
YOU HAVE YOUR HEAD
UP A DEAD ANIMAL.

116
00:05:25,366 --> 00:05:27,119
OOH, OH. MONICA.

117
00:05:30,831 --> 00:05:32,791
HEY.
HEY.

118
00:05:34,501 --> 00:05:35,543
HEY, DID YOU GET
THE TURKEY BASTE...?

119
00:05:35,543 --> 00:05:36,753
OH, MY GOD!

120
00:05:36,753 --> 00:05:38,463
OH, MY GOD!

121
00:05:38,463 --> 00:05:40,339
WHO IS THAT?

122
00:05:40,339 --> 00:05:42,843
IT'S JOEY.

123
00:05:42,843 --> 00:05:45,470
WHAT? WHAT ARE YOU DOING?
IS THIS SUPPOSED TO BE FUNNY?

124
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:46,930
NO, IT'S NOT SUPPOSED
TO BE FUNNY.

125
00:05:46,930 --> 00:05:49,975
IT'S SUPPOSED
TO BE SCARY.

126
00:05:49,975 --> 00:05:51,434
WELL, GET THAT
OFF NOW.

127
00:05:51,434 --> 00:05:53,478
I CAN'T. IT'S STUCK.

128
00:05:53,478 --> 00:05:56,231
I DON'T CARE. THAT HAS TO FEED
20 PEOPLE AT MY PARENTS' HOUSE

129
00:05:56,231 --> 00:05:58,317
AND THEY'RE NOT GOING TO EAT IT
OFF YOUR HEAD!

130
00:05:58,317 --> 00:05:59,651
HOLD ON, OKAY?

131
00:05:59,651 --> 00:06:01,653
LET'S JUST ALL THINK.

132
00:06:06,992 --> 00:06:08,827
OKAY, I GOT IT.

133
00:06:08,827 --> 00:06:10,954
PHOEBE, YOU PULL.

134
00:06:10,954 --> 00:06:13,915
I'M GOING TO SPREAD
THE LEGS AS WIDE AS I CAN.

135
00:06:13,915 --> 00:06:16,251
( snickering )

136
00:06:16,251 --> 00:06:17,252
JOEY?
YEAH.

137
00:06:17,252 --> 00:06:18,503
NOW IS NOT THE TIME.

138
00:06:18,503 --> 00:06:19,546
SORRY. RIGHT. SORRY.

139
00:06:19,546 --> 00:06:21,006
OKAY, ON THE COUNT OF THREE.

140
00:06:21,006 --> 00:06:23,884
ONE, TWO, THREE.

141
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:28,387
( yelling )

142
00:06:28,387 --> 00:06:29,973
IT WORKED.
I SCARED YOU.

143
00:06:29,973 --> 00:06:33,727
I KNEW IT.
HA-HA!

144
00:06:33,727 --> 00:06:34,811
I'M OVER HERE, BIG GUY.

145
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:36,938
YEAH, YOU ARE.
YEAH, HA-HA!

146
00:06:36,938 --> 00:06:38,940
I SCARED YOU.

147
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:40,984
( whooping )

148
00:06:42,277 --> 00:06:46,073
YOU-YOU DID LOOK LIKE AN IDIOT.

149
00:06:46,073 --> 00:06:48,616
HEY, I WASN'T THE ONLY ONE WHO
LOOKED LIKE AN IDIOT, ALL RIGHT?

150
00:06:48,616 --> 00:06:51,953
REMEMBER WHEN ROSS
TRIED TO SAY "BUTTERNUT SQUASH"

151
00:06:51,953 --> 00:06:53,830
AND IT CAME OUT...

152
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:55,414
"SQUATTER NUTBOSH"?

153
00:06:57,834 --> 00:06:59,878
YEAH, THAT'S
THE SAME.

154
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,882
WELL, THAT'S IT.
THAT'S MY WORST THANKSGIVING.

155
00:07:03,882 --> 00:07:06,927
OH, WAIT. THAT CAN'T BE THE ONE
THAT RACHEL WAS TALKING ABOUT

156
00:07:06,927 --> 00:07:09,470
'CAUSE SHE DIDN'T EVEN
KNOW THAT THAT HAPPENED.

157
00:07:09,470 --> 00:07:12,307
Joey: OH, RIGHT.
Ross: WHAT WAS IT?

158
00:07:12,307 --> 00:07:14,433
I-I REALLY DON'T WANT
TO TELL THIS STORY.

159
00:07:14,433 --> 00:07:17,104
OH, COME ON, MONICA.
RELIVING PAST PAIN
AND GETTING DEPRESSED

160
00:07:17,104 --> 00:07:20,607
IS WHAT THANKSGIVING'S
ALL ABOUT.

161
00:07:20,607 --> 00:07:22,067
YOU KNOW,
FOR ME ANYWAY.

162
00:07:22,067 --> 00:07:23,693
AND, OF COURSE,
THE INDIANS.

163
00:07:25,153 --> 00:07:26,363
LOOK, UM, OF ALL PEOPLE

164
00:07:26,363 --> 00:07:28,240
YOU DO NOT WANT ME
TO TELL THIS STORY.

165
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:30,284
WHAT IS THAT
SUPPOSED TO MEAN?

166
00:07:30,284 --> 00:07:33,453
( doorbell ringing )
MONICA! I THINK RACHEL IS HERE.

167
00:07:33,453 --> 00:07:34,579
Monica:
I'LL GET IT!

168
00:07:41,628 --> 00:07:43,462
HAPPY THANKSGIVING.

169
00:07:43,462 --> 00:07:45,048
NOT FOR ME.

170
00:07:45,048 --> 00:07:47,926
CHIP AND I BROKE UP.

171
00:07:47,926 --> 00:07:50,595
WHY? WHY? WELL,
WHAT HAPPENED?

172
00:07:50,595 --> 00:07:52,555
OH, YOU KNOW HOW
MY PARENTS ARE OUT OF TOWN

173
00:07:52,555 --> 00:07:53,974
AND CHIP WAS GOING
TO COME OVER?

174
00:07:53,974 --> 00:07:55,434
YEAH, YEAH, AND
YOU WERE GOING

175
00:07:55,434 --> 00:07:56,643
TO GIVE HIM,
YOU KNOW...

176
00:07:56,643 --> 00:07:59,229
YOUR FLOWER.

177
00:07:59,229 --> 00:08:01,440
OKAY, MONICA,
CAN YOU JUST CALL IT "SEX"?

178
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:04,692
IT REALLY CREEPS ME OUT
WHEN YOU CALL IT THAT.

179
00:08:04,692 --> 00:08:07,154
OKAY, AND BY THE WAY,
WHILE WE'RE AT IT

180
00:08:07,154 --> 00:08:10,031
A GUY'S THING IS NOT
CALLED HIS "TENDERNESS."

181
00:08:12,867 --> 00:08:14,702
BELIEVE ME.

182
00:08:16,496 --> 00:08:18,623
HI.
HI, RACHEL.

183
00:08:18,623 --> 00:08:20,708
HAPPY THANKSGIVING.
YOU TOO, SWEETHEART.

184
00:08:20,708 --> 00:08:22,043
HEY.

185
00:08:22,043 --> 00:08:24,463
OH, HI.

186
00:08:27,466 --> 00:08:28,883
UH... EVERYONE

187
00:08:28,883 --> 00:08:32,429
THIS IS CHANDLER,
MY ROOMMATE

188
00:08:32,429 --> 00:08:34,514
AND LEAD SINGER
OF OUR BAND.

189
00:08:37,017 --> 00:08:38,518
ROSS.

190
00:08:38,518 --> 00:08:40,520
OH, THIS IS MONICA.

191
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:43,064
HI, I'M ROSS'S
LITTLE SISTER.

192
00:08:43,064 --> 00:08:45,984
OKAY.

193
00:08:47,486 --> 00:08:49,654
I'M SO GLAD YOU COULD COME,
CHANDLER.

194
00:08:49,654 --> 00:08:52,032
WE GOT PLENTY OF FOOD,
SO I HOPE YOU'RE HUNGRY.

195
00:08:52,032 --> 00:08:54,117
OH, MOM, CHANDLER
HATES THANKSGIVING

196
00:08:54,117 --> 00:08:56,411
AND DOESN'T EAT ANY
THANKSGIVING FOOD.

197
00:08:56,411 --> 00:09:00,999
OH. OH, I'M SO GLAD
YOU BROUGHT HIM HERE, THEN.

198
00:09:00,999 --> 00:09:03,751
HEY, CHANDLER, UM...
IF YOU WANT, I CAN MAKE YOU

199
00:09:03,751 --> 00:09:05,712
SOME MACARONI
AND CHEESE FOR DINNER.

200
00:09:05,712 --> 00:09:07,881
WELL, AS LONG AS THE PILGRIMS
DIDN'T EAT IT, THEN I'M IN.

201
00:09:07,881 --> 00:09:09,632
( laughs, snorts soda )

202
00:09:12,010 --> 00:09:13,011
DAMN IT.

203
00:09:21,311 --> 00:09:23,563
SO, UH..., RACHE

204
00:09:23,563 --> 00:09:26,691
DOES IT, DOES IT FEEL
WEIRD AROUND HERE NOW?

205
00:09:26,691 --> 00:09:29,861
YOU KNOW, SINCE I'VE
BEEN AWAY AT COLLEGE?

206
00:09:29,861 --> 00:09:32,280
OH. NO, NOT REALLY.

207
00:09:33,365 --> 00:09:35,658
WELL, THAT'S COOL.

208
00:09:35,658 --> 00:09:36,617
SO DO...?

209
00:09:40,997 --> 00:09:42,040
OH!

210
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:44,584
I CANNOT BELIEVE
CHIP DUMPED ME

211
00:09:44,584 --> 00:09:47,170
FOR THAT SLUT 
NANCY BRANSON.

212
00:09:47,170 --> 00:09:48,629
I AM NEVER GOING OUT
WITH HIM AGAIN, YOU KNOW.

213
00:09:48,629 --> 00:09:51,632
I DON'T CARE HOW
MUCH HE BEGS.

214
00:09:51,632 --> 00:09:53,134
I THINK HIS BEGGING DAYS
ARE OVER

215
00:09:53,134 --> 00:09:54,844
NOW HE'S GOING OUT
WITH NANCY BRANSON.

216
00:09:57,013 --> 00:09:59,766
YOU KNOW WHAT?
I'VE JUST HAD IT
WITH HIGH SCHOOL BOYS.

217
00:09:59,766 --> 00:10:01,560
THEY'RE JUST... SILLY.

218
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:04,896
THEY'RE JUST SILLY,
STUPID BOYS.

219
00:10:04,896 --> 00:10:06,398
I'M GOING TO START DATING MEN.

220
00:10:07,690 --> 00:10:09,943
UH, I'M SORRY, JUDY.

221
00:10:09,943 --> 00:10:13,738
I COULDN'T FIND THAT BOWL
YOU AND JACK WERE LOOKING FOR.

222
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:18,617
( scoffs ): 
CALL THEM "MOM AND DAD,"
YOU LOSER.

223
00:10:20,828 --> 00:10:21,788
( whines ):
MONICA!

224
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:28,211
HEY, CHANDLER...

225
00:10:32,632 --> 00:10:34,259
DID YOU LIKE
THE MACARONI AND CHEESE?

226
00:10:34,259 --> 00:10:37,178
OH, YEAH. IT WAS GREAT.
YOU SHOULD BE A CHEF.

227
00:10:37,178 --> 00:10:39,139
OKAY.

228
00:10:42,517 --> 00:10:44,769
GUESS WHAT?
ALL THIS STUFF

229
00:10:44,769 --> 00:10:47,355
ABOUT NANCY BRANSON
BEING A SLUT WAS ALL A RUMOR,

230
00:10:47,355 --> 00:10:48,898
SO CHIP DUMPED HER

231
00:10:48,898 --> 00:10:50,900
AND HE WANTS TO COME OVER
TO MY HOUSE TONIGHT.

232
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,487
OH, THAT IS SO GREAT!

233
00:10:53,487 --> 00:10:54,821
OH, GOSH, LISTEN.

234
00:10:54,821 --> 00:10:57,031
IF YOU AND CHIP
DO IT TONIGHT

235
00:10:57,031 --> 00:10:59,409
PROMISE ME YOU'LL
TELL ME EVERYTHING.

236
00:10:59,409 --> 00:11:01,786
OH, TOTALLY, TOTALLY. YOU KNOW,
IT'S NOT THAT BIG A DEAL.

237
00:11:01,786 --> 00:11:03,497
WE ALREADY KIND OF
DID IT ONCE, YOU KNOW.

238
00:11:03,497 --> 00:11:05,248
I KNOW, BUT THIS
TIME YOU'RE GOING

239
00:11:05,248 --> 00:11:07,000
TO DEFINITELY KNOW
WHETHER OR NOT
YOU DID IT.

240
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,836
I KNOW. OH, AND CHIP PROMISED

241
00:11:09,836 --> 00:11:11,296
THAT-THAT THIS TIME
IT WOULD LAST

242
00:11:11,296 --> 00:11:13,548
AT LEAST FOR AN ENTIRE SONG.

243
00:11:15,883 --> 00:11:18,553
SO I'M THINKING OF ASKING
RACHEL OUT TONIGHT.

244
00:11:18,553 --> 00:11:19,971
YOU KNOW, MAYBE
PLAYING HER THAT SONG

245
00:11:19,971 --> 00:11:21,264
WE WROTE LAST WEEK.

246
00:11:21,264 --> 00:11:22,349
"EMOTIONAL KNAPSACK"?
YEAH.

247
00:11:22,349 --> 00:11:25,018
RIGHT ON.

248
00:11:25,018 --> 00:11:27,103
OH, BUT DON'T TAKE
TOO LONG, OKAY?

249
00:11:27,103 --> 00:11:28,647
BECAUSE, YOU KNOW,
WE'RE GOING TO TEST OUT

250
00:11:28,647 --> 00:11:31,732
OUR FAKE I.D.s TONIGHT,
RIGHT, CLIFFORD ALVEREZ?

251
00:11:33,401 --> 00:11:37,238
LISTEN, ROWLAND CHENG...

252
00:11:37,238 --> 00:11:40,408
IF THINGS GO WELL, I MAY
BE OUT WITH HER ALL NIGHT.

253
00:11:40,408 --> 00:11:42,827
DUDE, DON'T DO THAT TO ME.

254
00:11:42,827 --> 00:11:45,497
NO, IT'S COOL.
YOU CAN STAY HERE.
MY PARENTS WON'T MIND.

255
00:11:45,497 --> 00:11:47,374
NO, IT'S NOT THAT.
I JUST DON'T WANT
TO BE STUCK HERE

256
00:11:47,374 --> 00:11:48,583
ALL NIGHT WITH
YOUR FAT SISTER.

257
00:11:48,583 --> 00:11:49,584
HEY.

258
00:11:53,421 --> 00:11:55,590
MONICA, WHY DON'T YOU
FINISH OFF THESE PIES?

259
00:11:55,590 --> 00:11:58,134
I DON'T HAVE ANY MORE
ROOM IN THE FRIDGE.

260
00:12:00,178 --> 00:12:02,013
NO.

261
00:12:02,013 --> 00:12:04,265
NO, THANK YOU.

262
00:12:04,265 --> 00:12:05,684
WELL, JUDY, YOU DID IT.

263
00:12:05,684 --> 00:12:07,602
SHE'S FINALLY FULL.

264
00:12:12,357 --> 00:12:14,108
I CALLED YOU FAT?

265
00:12:14,108 --> 00:12:15,402
I DON'T EVEN
REMEMBER THAT.

266
00:12:15,402 --> 00:12:16,611
WELL, I DO.

267
00:12:16,611 --> 00:12:19,113
I'M SO SORRY.
I REALLY AM.

268
00:12:19,113 --> 00:12:20,739
BUT, COME ON, I WAS
AN IDIOT BACK THEN.

269
00:12:20,739 --> 00:12:22,659
I RUSHED THE STAGE
AT A WHAM! CONCERT,

270
00:12:22,659 --> 00:12:25,620
FOR CRYING OUT LOUD.

271
00:12:25,620 --> 00:12:27,664
OH, I CAN'T BELIEVE
YOU CALLED HER FAT.

272
00:12:27,664 --> 00:12:31,084
I CAN'T BELIEVE YOU LET
GEORGE MICHAEL SLAP YOU.

273
00:12:32,544 --> 00:12:33,878
I AM REALLY SORRY.

274
00:12:33,878 --> 00:12:35,088
THAT IS SO TERRIBLE.

275
00:12:35,088 --> 00:12:37,340
I'M SO, SO SORRY.

276
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:40,260
ACTUALLY, YOU KNOW,
THAT'S NOT THE THANKSGIVING
I WAS TALKING ABOUT.

277
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:43,137
YES, IT WAS.
NO, IT WASN'T.
IT WAS ACTUALLY...

278
00:12:43,137 --> 00:12:44,598
THANKSGIVING'S OVER.
LET'S GET READY FOR CHRISTMAS.

279
00:12:44,598 --> 00:12:47,766
WHO WANTS TO GO GET
A CHRISTMAS TREE?

280
00:12:47,766 --> 00:12:51,145
OOH, NO. I HAVE THE
CUTEST CHRISTMAS STORY.

281
00:12:51,145 --> 00:12:53,189
BUT WE WANT
TO HEAR MONICA'S
THANKSGIVING STORY.

282
00:12:53,189 --> 00:12:54,857
FINE. ALL RIGHT.
MINE HAD A DWARF

283
00:12:54,857 --> 00:12:57,235
THAT GOT BROKE IN HALF
BUT, YOU KNOW, WHATEVER.

284
00:12:59,237 --> 00:13:02,532
SO, RACHEL, YOUR MOM TELLS ME
YOU CHANGED YOUR MAJOR AGAIN.

285
00:13:02,532 --> 00:13:04,909
WELL, YEAH, I HAD TO.
THERE WAS NEVER ANY PARKING

286
00:13:04,909 --> 00:13:07,954
BY THE PSYCHOLOGY BUILDING.

287
00:13:07,954 --> 00:13:09,623
HI, RACHEL.
OH, HI.

288
00:13:09,623 --> 00:13:11,832
WOW, LOVE
YOUR NEW NOSE.

289
00:13:11,832 --> 00:13:13,167
JACK...

290
00:13:13,167 --> 00:13:15,462
WHAT? DR. WILSON'S
AN ARTIST.

291
00:13:15,462 --> 00:13:17,130
HE REMOVED MY MOLE CLUSTER.

292
00:13:17,130 --> 00:13:18,673
WANT TO SEE?

293
00:13:18,673 --> 00:13:19,966
( doorbell rings )
I'LL GET IT.

294
00:13:19,966 --> 00:13:22,260
NO, GOD. PLEASE LET ME.

295
00:13:25,388 --> 00:13:27,265
HEY.
HEY.

296
00:13:30,685 --> 00:13:33,647
HAPPY THANKSGIVING.
HI.

297
00:13:33,647 --> 00:13:35,607
GOD, YOUR HAIR
SURE IS DIFFERENT.

298
00:13:35,607 --> 00:13:37,400
YEAH, WE WERE JUST TALKING
ABOUT THAT.

299
00:13:37,400 --> 00:13:39,068
I CAN'T BELIEVE
HOW STUPID WE USED TO LOOK.

300
00:13:39,068 --> 00:13:40,027
YEAH.

301
00:13:43,615 --> 00:13:45,325
SO, UH, WHERE'S MONICA?

302
00:13:45,325 --> 00:13:46,534
SHE'S UPSTAIRS.

303
00:13:46,534 --> 00:13:48,119
MONICA, COME DOWN.

304
00:13:48,119 --> 00:13:50,664
EVERYONE'S HERE--
ROSS, RACHEL

305
00:13:50,664 --> 00:13:52,666
AND THE BOY
WHO HATES THANKSGIVING.

306
00:13:56,336 --> 00:13:58,672
HI, CHANDLER.

307
00:13:58,672 --> 00:14:00,839
OH, MY GOD.

308
00:14:00,839 --> 00:14:02,676
W-W-WHAT'S THE MATTER?
IS THERE...

309
00:14:02,676 --> 00:14:06,554
IS THERE SOMETHING
ON MY DRESS?

310
00:14:06,554 --> 00:14:10,016
YOU LOOK SO DIFFERENT,
TERRIFIC.

311
00:14:10,016 --> 00:14:11,685
THAT DRESS, THAT BODY.

312
00:14:11,685 --> 00:14:13,186
DUDE.
SORRY.

313
00:14:14,521 --> 00:14:15,938
YES, YES. MONICA IS THIN.

314
00:14:15,938 --> 00:14:17,273
IT'S WONDERFUL,

315
00:14:17,273 --> 00:14:18,941
BUT WHAT WE REALLY
WANT TO HEAR ABOUT

316
00:14:18,941 --> 00:14:20,694
IS ROSS'S NEW GIRLFRIEND.

317
00:14:20,694 --> 00:14:22,278
OH, MOM.

318
00:14:22,278 --> 00:14:25,573
OKAY. UM,
HER NAME IS CAROL

319
00:14:25,573 --> 00:14:27,659
AND SHE'S REALLY PRETTY
AND SMART

320
00:14:27,659 --> 00:14:30,161
AND, UH, SHE'S...
SHE'S ON THE LACROSSE TEAM

321
00:14:30,161 --> 00:14:32,831
AND THE GOLF TEAM,
CAN YOU BELIEVE IT?

322
00:14:32,831 --> 00:14:34,957
SHE PLAYS FOR BOTH TEAMS.

323
00:14:37,502 --> 00:14:39,713
SO, CHANDLER, I GUESS
I'LL SEE YOU AT DINNER.

324
00:14:41,881 --> 00:14:43,216
DUDE.
SORRY.

325
00:14:45,218 --> 00:14:48,304
OH, MY GOD. THAT
WAS SO AWESOME.

326
00:14:48,304 --> 00:14:50,765
YOU TOTALLY GOT HIM BACK
FOR CALLING YOU FAT.

327
00:14:50,765 --> 00:14:52,559
HE WAS JUST DROOLING
ALL OVER YOU.

328
00:14:52,559 --> 00:14:54,268
THAT MUST HAVE
FELT SO GREAT.

329
00:14:54,268 --> 00:14:55,353
WELL, IT DIDN'T.

330
00:14:55,353 --> 00:14:56,437
WHAT?

331
00:14:56,437 --> 00:14:59,399
YEAH. I MEAN,
YEAH, I LOOK GREAT

332
00:14:59,399 --> 00:15:01,067
AND, YEAH, I FEEL GREAT,
AND, YEAH, MY HEART'S

333
00:15:01,067 --> 00:15:04,904
NOT IN TROUBLE ANYMORE,
BLAH, BLAH, BLAH.

334
00:15:04,904 --> 00:15:07,490
I JUST DON'T FEEL
LIKE I GOT HIM BACK, YOU KNOW?

335
00:15:07,490 --> 00:15:09,784
I JUST WANT TO HUMILIATE HIM.
I WANT TO...

336
00:15:09,784 --> 00:15:12,203
I WANT HIM TO BE LIKE NAKED
AND I WANT TO POINT AT HIM

337
00:15:12,203 --> 00:15:14,622
AND I WANT TO LAUGH.

338
00:15:14,622 --> 00:15:15,915
OKAY.

339
00:15:15,915 --> 00:15:19,669
THAT WE MAY
BE ABLE TO DO.

340
00:15:19,669 --> 00:15:20,837
HOW?

341
00:15:20,837 --> 00:15:22,672
WELL, GUYS
TEND TO GET NAKED

342
00:15:22,672 --> 00:15:24,758
BEFORE THEY'RE
GOING TO HAVE SEX.

343
00:15:24,758 --> 00:15:26,676
WHAT?!

344
00:15:26,676 --> 00:15:28,720
I DIDN'T WORK THIS HARD
A-A-AND LOSE ALL THIS WEIGHT

345
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:32,139
JUST SO I COULD GIVE MY FLOWER
TO SOMEONE LIKE HIM.

346
00:15:32,139 --> 00:15:34,475
OKAY, FIRST OF ALL, IF
YOU KEEP CALLING IT THAT

347
00:15:34,475 --> 00:15:36,227
NO ONE'S EVER
GOING TO TAKE IT.

348
00:15:36,227 --> 00:15:38,605
AND THEN,
SECOND OF ALL

349
00:15:38,605 --> 00:15:40,189
YOU'RE NOT GOING TO ACTUALLY
HAVE SEX WITH HIM.

350
00:15:40,189 --> 00:15:41,399
YOU'RE JUST GOING
TO MAKE HIM THINK

351
00:15:41,399 --> 00:15:43,693
THAT YOU ARE.

352
00:15:43,693 --> 00:15:45,612
YEAH.

353
00:15:45,612 --> 00:15:47,864
AND THEN WHEN HE'S NAKED,
I CAN THROW HIM OUT
IN THE FRONT YARD

354
00:15:47,864 --> 00:15:49,866
AND LOCK THE DOOR,
AND THEN ALL OUR NEIGHBORS

355
00:15:49,866 --> 00:15:51,785
WILL JUST HUMILIATE HIM.

356
00:15:51,785 --> 00:15:54,370
YEAH, AND THEN YOU WILL
DEFINITELY GET HIM BACK.

357
00:15:54,370 --> 00:15:56,706
HOW DO I MAKE HIM THINK
I WANT TO HAVE SEX WITH HIM?

358
00:15:56,706 --> 00:15:58,917
UH, HERE'S
WHAT YOU DO.

359
00:15:58,917 --> 00:16:03,546
JUST ACT LIKE EVERYTHING
AROUND YOU TURNS YOU ON.

360
00:16:06,048 --> 00:16:08,760
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?
WELL, LIKE ANYTHING
CAN BE SEXY,

361
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:10,052
LIKE, UM...

362
00:16:10,052 --> 00:16:12,722
OH! OKAY, LIKE THIS...
LIKE THIS DISHTOWEL.

363
00:16:12,722 --> 00:16:16,309
OOH... OOH...

364
00:16:16,309 --> 00:16:19,729
THIS FEELS SO GOOD
AGAINST MY CHEEK.

365
00:16:19,729 --> 00:16:24,525
AND IF I GET A LITTLE HOT,
I CAN JUST DAB MYSELF WITH IT.

366
00:16:24,525 --> 00:16:26,486
OR I CAN BRING IT
DOWN TO MY SIDE

367
00:16:26,486 --> 00:16:28,154
AND MAYBE RUN IT
THROUGH MY FINGERS

368
00:16:28,154 --> 00:16:29,864
WHILE I TALK TO HIM.

369
00:16:29,864 --> 00:16:31,240
I CAN DO THAT.

370
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:32,951
YEAH? OKAY, GOOD, GOOD.

371
00:16:32,951 --> 00:16:35,662
HE'S COMING.
HE'S COMING.

372
00:16:35,662 --> 00:16:37,455
HEY, WHAT'S UP?
HEY.

373
00:16:39,332 --> 00:16:40,875
MONICA, I WAS WONDERING
IF YOU COULD MAKE ME

374
00:16:40,875 --> 00:16:42,418
SOME OF THAT RIGHTEOUS
MAC 'N' CHEESE

375
00:16:42,418 --> 00:16:44,128
LIKE LAST YEAR.

376
00:16:44,128 --> 00:16:45,797
UH, I'D LOVE TO.

377
00:16:51,719 --> 00:16:55,473
OOH... I LOVE 
MACARONI AND CHEESE.

378
00:16:57,809 --> 00:16:59,602
I LOVE... I LOVE
THE WAY THIS BOX FEELS

379
00:16:59,602 --> 00:17:01,270
AGAINST MY CHEEK.

380
00:17:07,485 --> 00:17:08,486
OKAY.

381
00:17:08,486 --> 00:17:10,237
OH, AND I LOVE CARROTS.

382
00:17:10,237 --> 00:17:11,948
OH...

383
00:17:14,241 --> 00:17:17,161
SOMETIMES I LIKE TO PUT THEM
BETWEEN MY FINGERS...

384
00:17:19,372 --> 00:17:22,040
LIKE THIS, AND... AND...
AND HOLD THEM DOWN HERE

385
00:17:22,040 --> 00:17:24,002
WHILE I TALK TO YOU.

386
00:17:28,506 --> 00:17:31,091
UM, AN-AN-AND YOU KNOW,
IF I GET REALLY HOT?

387
00:17:31,091 --> 00:17:34,053
UM, I-I LIKE TO...

388
00:17:34,053 --> 00:17:35,179
PICK UP THIS KNIFE

389
00:17:35,179 --> 00:17:37,139
AND... AND, UM,

390
00:17:37,139 --> 00:17:40,810
I PUT THE...
THE COOL STEEL

391
00:17:40,810 --> 00:17:43,229
AGAINST, UM...

392
00:17:43,229 --> 00:17:45,023
MY BODY.

393
00:17:46,524 --> 00:17:48,150
ARE YOU ALL RIGHT?

394
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:50,444
OH, YEAH, YEAH.
I'M FINE. IT'S...

395
00:18:05,752 --> 00:18:07,545
WHAT HAVE WE GOT HERE?
20-YEAR-OLD MALE.

396
00:18:07,545 --> 00:18:10,172
HE'S GOT A SEVERED TOE
ON HIS RIGHT FOOT.

397
00:18:10,172 --> 00:18:12,550
OW! OW!

398
00:18:12,550 --> 00:18:14,886
COULD YOU PLEASE NOT
DO THAT FEET-FIRST?

399
00:18:14,886 --> 00:18:16,679
YOU KNOW
WHERE HIS INJURY IS.

400
00:18:16,679 --> 00:18:18,389
SEVERED TOE.
YOU JUST SAID IT!

401
00:18:20,224 --> 00:18:22,476
SAYS HERE THE KNIFE
WENT RIGHT THROUGH YOUR SHOE.

402
00:18:22,476 --> 00:18:25,521
OF COURSE IT DID.
THEY'RE MADE OF WICKER.

403
00:18:25,521 --> 00:18:26,856
DID YOU BRING
THE TOE?

404
00:18:26,856 --> 00:18:30,359
OH, YES. I HAVE IT
RIGHT HERE ON ICE.

405
00:18:30,359 --> 00:18:33,529
DON'T WORRY, SON, WE'LL
JUST REATTACH IT AND THEN...

406
00:18:33,529 --> 00:18:35,031
WHAT? WHAT IS IT?

407
00:18:35,031 --> 00:18:36,824
YOU BROUGHT A CARROT.

408
00:18:38,409 --> 00:18:39,786
WHAT?

409
00:18:39,786 --> 00:18:41,579
THIS ISN'T YOUR TOE.
THIS IS A SMALL,

410
00:18:41,579 --> 00:18:44,082
VERY COLD PIECE OF CARROT.

411
00:18:44,082 --> 00:18:46,166
YOU BROUGHT
A CARROT?

412
00:18:46,166 --> 00:18:48,252
OH, MY GOD.

413
00:18:48,252 --> 00:18:50,546
THERE'S A TOE
IN MY KITCHEN.

414
00:18:52,506 --> 00:18:54,383
GOD, I'M SORRY!
I'LL GO BACK AND GET IT!

415
00:18:54,383 --> 00:18:56,552
IT'S TOO LATE. ALL WE CAN DO NOW
IS SEW UP THE WOUND.

416
00:18:56,552 --> 00:18:59,013
WITHOUT MY TOE?
I NEED MY TOE.

417
00:18:59,013 --> 00:19:01,015
WHAT? NO, NO.
I CAN GO REALLY FAST.

418
00:19:01,015 --> 00:19:02,433
DAD, GIVE ME THE
KEYS TO YOUR PORSCHE.

419
00:19:02,433 --> 00:19:06,353
OH, I'M NOT FALLING
FOR THAT ONE.

420
00:19:06,353 --> 00:19:08,064
THAT'S WHY I LOST MY TOE?

421
00:19:08,064 --> 00:19:09,482
BECAUSE I CALLED YOU FAT?

422
00:19:11,567 --> 00:19:14,320
I DIDN'T MEAN TO CUT IT OFF.
IT WAS AN ACCIDENT.

423
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:15,780
THAT'S WHY, FOR AN ENTIRE YEAR

424
00:19:15,780 --> 00:19:19,158
PEOPLE CALLED ME
SIR LIMPS-A-LOT?

425
00:19:19,158 --> 00:19:21,619
I'M SORRY.

426
00:19:21,619 --> 00:19:23,329
IT WASN'T YOUR WHOLE TOE.

427
00:19:23,329 --> 00:19:25,665
YEAH, WELL,
I MISS THE TIP.

428
00:19:25,665 --> 00:19:28,375
IT'S THE BEST PART.

429
00:19:28,375 --> 00:19:29,752
IT HAS THE NAIL.

430
00:19:31,963 --> 00:19:33,131
CHANDLER...

431
00:19:35,257 --> 00:19:39,137
SIR LIMPS-A-LOT--
I CAME UP WITH THAT.

432
00:19:41,055 --> 00:19:43,683
YOU'RE A DORK.

433
00:19:43,683 --> 00:19:45,685
( sighing ):
I CAN'T BELIEVE THIS.

434
00:19:45,685 --> 00:19:47,103
CHANDLER, I SAID
I WAS SORRY.

435
00:19:47,103 --> 00:19:48,646
YEAH? WELL, SORRY
DOESN'T BRING BACK

436
00:19:48,646 --> 00:19:50,815
THE LITTLE PIGGY
THAT CRIED ALL THE WAY HOME.

437
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:56,529
I HATE THIS STUPID DAY
AND EVERYTHING ABOUT IT.

438
00:19:56,529 --> 00:19:58,656
I'LL SEE YOU LATER.
OH, WAIT, CHANDLER.

439
00:19:58,656 --> 00:20:02,118
COME HERE. IS THERE
ANYTHING I CAN DO?

440
00:20:02,118 --> 00:20:03,661
ANYTHING?

441
00:20:03,661 --> 00:20:06,330
YEAH, JUST... LEAVE ME ALONE
FOR A LITTLE WHILE.

442
00:20:13,087 --> 00:20:15,131
OH, OH, I'M A DUCK.
I GO, "QUACK, QUACK."

443
00:20:15,131 --> 00:20:16,924
I'M HAPPY ALL THE TIME.

444
00:20:16,924 --> 00:20:18,592
( knocking )

445
00:20:28,019 --> 00:20:29,603
NICE TRY.

446
00:20:29,603 --> 00:20:30,938
WAIT, WAIT, WAIT, WAIT.

447
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:35,735
LOOK, MONICA...

448
00:20:40,073 --> 00:20:41,741
THIS IS NOT GOING TO WORK.

449
00:20:41,741 --> 00:20:43,034
I BET THIS WILL WORK.

450
00:20:46,829 --> 00:20:48,122
( laughing )

451
00:20:51,918 --> 00:20:55,171
YOU ARE SO GREAT.
I LOVE YOU.

452
00:21:03,971 --> 00:21:05,890
WHAT?

453
00:21:05,890 --> 00:21:07,641
NOTHING. I SAID...
I SAID, "YOU'RE SO GREAT,"

454
00:21:07,641 --> 00:21:09,852
AND THEN I JUST...
I JUST STOPPED TALKING.

455
00:21:11,938 --> 00:21:13,856
YOU SAID YOU LOVED ME.
I CAN'T BELIEVE THIS.

456
00:21:13,856 --> 00:21:16,817
NO, I DIDN'T.

457
00:21:16,817 --> 00:21:18,027
YES, YOU DID.

458
00:21:18,027 --> 00:21:19,445
NO, I DIDN'T.

459
00:21:19,445 --> 00:21:21,864
YOU LOVE ME.

460
00:21:21,864 --> 00:21:23,199
NO, I DON'T!

461
00:21:23,199 --> 00:21:25,451
STOP IT! STOP IT!
STOP IT! STOP IT!

462
00:21:25,451 --> 00:21:28,079
( screaming )

463
00:21:38,297 --> 00:21:40,716
GAUZE! GAUZE!

464
00:21:40,716 --> 00:21:43,552
I NEED TO GET
SOME GAUZE IN HERE!

465
00:21:43,552 --> 00:21:45,930
CAN I PLEASE GET
